      <groundspeak:long_description html="True"> </groundspeak:long_description>
      <groundspeak:encoded_hints>IN W/V CVR IN S/W 7.7M NE SIGN

BCP758-BBB Event. Elevation 905.854 m IN A WATER VALVE COVER IN THE SIDEWALK 7.7M NE OF &quot;STOP&quot; SIGN POST; 0.18M N OF B.O.W.SCENIC DR Scenic Drive</groundspeak:encoded_hints>
      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="1332982858">
          <groundspeak:date>2025-11-02T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="25790230">MaybeSunshine</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP758 BBB Event [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Maybe I just got lucky on this trip, but every cap I looked for in Lethbridge over the past couple of days was dead simple. Similar to some other finders here, I removed the obvious cover and could sort of see the cap below a thin layer of grime and ice. I called it good. Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="711433724">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-08-13T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="181446">DanOCan</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP758:  BBB Event [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;My first trip down to Lethbridge since January.  Before leaving town to head home, Tucker the Dog and I needed to do some capping.  We only looked for two, but both were a success.  This one's hidey hole was easy to spot and I could even pop the lid off without needing my small pry bar, which I had left at home anyway.  I opted to not reach way down and clean off the cap itself since it looked like  something best done while wearing gloves.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="687915183">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-21T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="228846">Mr. CanoeHead</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP758 BBB Event (FOUND)

A quiet Sunday Morning was a good time to go for this one.  Quickly located the cover in the side walk and then peered deep into the abyss to spot the cap at the bottom of the hole.  Cap was in pretty bad shape despite its protective hole and covering.   TFTCap&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684678912">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3061435">Iron Phoenix</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP758 - BBB Event&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Out for yet another day of capping and caching with OBA, this time in Lethbridge!! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Along the way there and back. &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_wink.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; A quick pop of the cover and a flash on the camera and we were on our way to the next one! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Might not have gotten all the numbers in the picture, but I couldn't reach it to wipe it clean. &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_sad.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; TFTCap!!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684656165">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="540154">One Bad Ant</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP758 - BBB Event  - a grey day to be capping in Lethbridge, lots of lovely places and a little rain. Thanks OFTH for maintaining the brass cap cache.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
